                <mxCell id="gndbus" value="" style="rounded=1;fillColor=#212121;strokeColor=#616161;shadow=1;arcSize=10;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="60" y="560" width="1120" height="30" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="gndbusl" value="&lt;b style='color:#E0E0E0;font-size:12px'&gt;COMMON GND BUS — Jetson GND + 12V PSU GND + module DC− / control GND&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="60" y="564" width="1120" height="22" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>

                <mxCell id="steps" value="&lt;b style='font-size:13px;color:#0D47A1'&gt;Step-by-step: → MOSFET module&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Buy:&lt;/b&gt; a &lt;b&gt;dual-MOSFET trigger switch driver module&lt;/b&gt; (D4184-class, DC 5–36V, 15A/400W) whose spec lists a &lt;b&gt;3.3–20V digital trigger&lt;/b&gt; (e.g. Seloky dual-MOS board). Avoid IRF520 boards (need 4–5V, won't fully turn on at 3.3V). Plus a &lt;b&gt;1N5408&lt;/b&gt; (3A) flyback diode. NOTE: the trigger pin may be labeled &lt;b&gt;PWM&lt;/b&gt; or &lt;b&gt;TRIG&lt;/b&gt; — that is SIG.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;1.&lt;/b&gt; Power OFF (Jetson + 12V supply).&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;2. REMOVE&lt;/b&gt; the IRLB8721 MOSFET, the 4.7kΩ pull-up (and any 1kΩ), and the T17 (+3.3V) wire — none are used.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;3. MOVE the GREEN wire&lt;/b&gt; from the old gate junction to the module's &lt;b&gt;SIG&lt;/b&gt; input. (Source stays T13 / BCM 27 — same pin, no software change.)&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;4.&lt;/b&gt; Module &lt;b&gt;control GND → Jetson GND&lt;/b&gt; (shared reference — REQUIRED, or SIG won't be seen). VCC control pin: leave open (it only lights the LED) or tie to +3.3V.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;5.&lt;/b&gt; &lt;b&gt;+12V → DC+&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b&gt;GND → DC−&lt;/b&gt; (power-in screw terminals).&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;6.&lt;/b&gt; &lt;b&gt;OUT+ → solenoid (+) RED&lt;/b&gt;, &lt;b&gt;OUT− → solenoid (−) BLUE&lt;/b&gt; (the module switches the low side).&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;7.&lt;/b&gt; &lt;b&gt;1N5408 flyback&lt;/b&gt; across the solenoid coil — band (cathode) to the (+)/OUT+ side. (Use the 3A 1N5408, not the 1N4007, for a 2A coil.)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style='color:#1B5E20'&gt;&lt;b&gt;Software:&lt;/b&gt; unchanged. Keep the &lt;b&gt;libgpiod 3.3V drive&lt;/b&gt; on BCM 27 — the D4184 gate threshold is ~2V, so 3.3V switches it fully; the weak ~1.6V Jetson.GPIO would NOT. HIGH → solenoid opens. The D4184 at 2A dissipates ~0.02W → runs stone cold.&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#E3F2FD;strokeColor=#1976D2;fontColor=#333;fontSize=11;strokeWidth=2;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;spacingTop=10;spacingBottom=10;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="60" y="620" width="1120" height="320" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
            </root>
        </mxGraphModel>
    </diagram>
</mxfile>
